{"content":[{"c":["ARAM-NAHARAIM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Hebrew word meaning “Aram of the two rivers”; it refers to the area bounded by the upper Euphrates and the Habur Rivers. It is sometimes translated “Mesopotamia” (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.23.4","r":"Deut.23.4","rawR":"Deut.23.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.23.4","value":"Deut.23.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 23:4"},", ",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). The major city of that area was Haran, where Terah and Abram stopped and where Terah died (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.11.31-32","r":"Gen.11.31-32","rawR":"Gen.11.31-32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.11.31-32","value":"Gen.11.31-32"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 11:31-32"},"). A servant of Abraham (Abram) returned to the same region to seek a wife for Abraham’s son Isaac (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.24.1-10","r":"Gen.24.1-10","rawR":"Gen.24.1-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.24.1-10","value":"Gen.24.1-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 24:1-10"},"). Isaac’s son Jacob also returned to Haran to seek a wife (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.28.1-5","r":"Gen.28.1-5","rawR":"Gen.28.1-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.28.1-5","value":"Gen.28.1-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 28:1-5"},"; Paddan-aram is a synonym of Aram-naharaim). Aram-naharaim was the home of Balaam, the pagan prophet (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.23.4","r":"Deut.23.4","rawR":"Deut.23.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.23.4","value":"Deut.23.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 23:4"},"). One oppressor of Israel during the period of the judges was Cushan-rishathaim, king of Aram-naharaim (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.3.8-11","r":"Judg.3.8-11","rawR":"Judg.3.8-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.3.8-11","value":"Judg.3.8-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 3:8-11"},"). Later, in King David’s wars with Ammon, he had to confront mercenary charioteers hired from the Aramean centers of Aram-naharaim, Aram-maacah, and Zobah (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.19.6","r":"1Chr.19.6","rawR":"1Chr.19.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.19.6","value":"1Chr.19.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 19:6"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.60.1","r":"Ps.60.1","rawR":"Ps.60.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.60.1","value":"Ps.60.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 60 title"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=SyriaSyrians_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"SyriaSyrians_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"SyriaSyrians_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Syria, Syrians"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"AramNaharaim","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Dt 23:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.23.4","rawQueryValue":"Deut.23.4","sourceRefExact":"Deut.23.4"},{"anchorText":"Gn 11:31-32","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.11.31-32","rawQueryValue":"Gen.11.31-32","sourceRefExact":"Gen.11.31-32"},{"anchorText":"Gn 24:1-10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.24.1-10","rawQueryValue":"Gen.24.1-10","sourceRefExact":"Gen.24.1-10"},{"anchorText":"Gn 28:1-5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.28.1-5","rawQueryValue":"Gen.28.1-5","sourceRefExact":"Gen.28.1-5"},{"anchorText":"Dt 23:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.23.4","rawQueryValue":"Deut.23.4","sourceRefExact":"Deut.23.4"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 3:8-11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.3.8-11","rawQueryValue":"Judg.3.8-11","sourceRefExact":"Judg.3.8-11"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 19:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.19.6","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.19.6","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.19.6"},{"anchorText":"Ps 60 title","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.60.1","rawQueryValue":"Ps.60.1","sourceRefExact":"Ps.60.1"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"702d72976bfec8f3310e0a68ef4af32d570ad278b38278422f75d2185e7a5e6e","sourceItemName":"AramNaharaim","sourceItemOrder":442,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"AramNaharaim","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Aram-Naharaim","title":"Aram-Naharaim","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}